I was really intruiged about Power Systems because of my Power Lab so I wanted to better understand the theory by putting it into practice. It helped me better understand how shunt
capacitors  and transformers tap settings affect bus voltages and why both voltage and equipment loading need to be checked when evaluating a case. The biggest takeaway from 
all of this was that a seemingly fine power flow network can be operating in undesired way and have voltage and loading problems. Contingency analysis helped me better understand 
the weaknesses which stayed hidden when  everything was normal and it taught me to explain the limitations of my results alongside the improvements I made.
